From 7995fcdff8d97c8f82cacd79d8a9ad06030a4166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:42:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add an Obsidian dark theme with a footer light/dark switch

The site now follows the visitor's device setting (dark or light) until they
pick one with the sun/moon switch in the footer; the choice is remembered.
A head script sets data-theme before first paint, so there is no flash.

Dark theme ("Obsidian"): black ground, white Work Sans headings at 500,
#cbcbcb body, one blue accent (#6289ff), smoked-glass nav capsule, cards
with a gradient hairline edge instead of shadows, squarer corners, white
buttons with a blue arrow chip, blue eyebrows between diamond-ended rules,
a lit black closing poster and a footer with grey and blue glows. Status
badges, forms, tabs, the how-we-work sheet and the visa checker are tuned
for black. Light theme is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HfgsaJsCawzUVu4y2jiGHK
